Assistant: The error indicates that `durationConfig.includes` is being called but `durationConfig` is not an array as expected. Looking at the preview file, we're passing an empty object as `mockDurationConfig`, but based on the error and usage, it should be an array.

Let's fix this by modifying the preview file to provide a proper durationConfig array:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/Type-8ae77e7c.tsx">
  <change>
    <description>Update mockDurationConfig to be an array instead of an empty object</description>
    <content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import ImportedComponent from '../../modules/d/[link]/d-type-view';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    slug: {
      type: "string",
      value: "example-event",
      label: "Slug",
    },
    isEmbed: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Embed",
    },
    user: {
      type: "string",
      value: "johndoe",
      label: "User",
    },
    isBrandingHidden: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Branding Hidden",
    },
    isTeamEvent: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Team Event",
    },
    duration: {
      type: "number",
      value: 60,
      label: "Duration",
    },
    hashedLink: {
      type: "string",
      value: "abc123",
      label: "Hashed Link",
    },
  });

  // Mock objects for complex props
  const mockBooking = {};
  const mockEntity = {};
  // Update durationConfig to be an array with common duration values
  const mockDurationConfig = [15, 30, 45, 60];

  return (
    <ImportedComponent
      slug={state.slug.value}
      isEmbed={state.isEmbed.value}
      user={state.user.value}
      booking={mockBooking}
      isBrandingHidden={state.isBrandingHidden.value}
      isTeamEvent={state.isTeamEvent.value}
      entity={mockEntity}
      duration={state.duration.value}
      hashedLink={state.hashedLink.value}
      durationConfig={mockDurationConfig}
    />
  );
}
</content>
  </change>
</file>

I've updated the `mockDurationConfig` to be an array instead of an empty object. The array contains common duration values (15, 30, 45, 60 minutes) that are typically used in booking systems. This should resolve the error since the `includes()` method is available on arrays but not on plain objects.

The error was occurring because somewhere in the component tree, there's code trying to call `durationConfig.includes()` to check if a specific duration is included in the allowed durations. By providing an actual array, this method call will now work as expected.

